# tflw `M242` `G` (`D1332`) — the cookbook's feature-flag pattern, kept true by this file.
#
# The language has no conditionals, so a feature behind a flag is not an `if` in a test: the tests
# that need the flag on carry a tag naming it, and the job that runs with the flag off leaves them
# out on the command line —
#
#     tflw run --tag !flag_giftMessage
#
# — which `verify-cli-flags.mjs` proves against the same run without the exclusion. The test below
# is the flagged half; the known-answer route stands in for the feature.
@cookbook @flag_giftMessage
test "the gift-message flag's test runs only where the flag is on"
  api GET /soft-check/known-answer
  expect status equals 200
  expect body.label equals "known-answer"
